language-derived-from-the-record-4 = unlines (cons "**2. Occurrences and identification.** A participant i of the universe's process receives it only through its observation, and its record R_i is everything it has received. An occurrence of a word w is an event of i's record R_i that i identifies as w. Identification is i's act on its record, since no two sound waves are equal. So for i a word is a type Occ_i(w): its points are events of the record, its paths are i's identifications of them. Every occurrence e has a context c(e) ∈ C, the record around it, which is itself made of occurrences and percepts and so carries the same structure one level up." nil)
